  "title": "Kaʻahumanu",
  "summary": "A high-ranking Hawaiian woman born on Maui and favored wife of Kamehameha I, she became the first kuhina nui (co-ruler) after his death in 1819 and queen regent from 1823. She helped end the ʻai kapu eating restrictions, issued a law code in 1824 and put down a rebellion on Kauaʻi. She died in 1832.",
